# The guard is bash. On Windows, core.autocrlf would hand it CRLF line endings
# and bash would fail with `$'\r': command not found`. This is the one-line fix.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.md        text

# STATE.md is append-at-the-top by every session, from every machine. Union
# merge keeps BOTH sides of a concurrent append instead of raising a conflict.
#
# Caveat, and it is a real one: union merge also keeps both sides when two
# people edit the SAME queue row. You get a visibly duplicated row, not a
# silently wrong one — fix it by hand and move on. That trade is deliberate:
# a duplicate line you can see beats a merge conflict on every single push.
docs/STATE.md merge=union
